# shipping.config — THE SHIPPING CONFIGURATION, IN ONE PLACE.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS
#
# On 2026-09-09 the build that ships was found not to be the build that was
# measured, in three independent parameters at once (findings S8-2, S9-1):
#
#   * BLOCK.  PW ruled on 2026-09-03 that block 16 is the configuration that
#     fits both chips -- block 8 is 116.4 % of chip 1's budget and 104.9 % of
#     chip 2's and never fitted either. The ruling was applied only inside the
#     measurement scripts, which build a scratch tree with DSP4_GEN_BLOCK=16.
#     The committed tree has been generated at BLOCK=8 since 2026-08-28 and
#     `./build.sh` has always produced a block-8 image.
#   * BLOCK KERNELS.  Every capacity figure since 2026-09-01, the `.4` record
#     included, is a DSP4_BLOCK_KERNELS=1 build. The build default was 0.
#   * CORE CLOCK.  Every cycle budget since 2026-08-24 is quoted at 983.04 MHz
#     on the strength of PW's U5/U6 part reading (ADSP-21564KSWZ10, the 1 GHz
#     grade). The build default was DSP4_CCLK_TARGET=0, which leaves the CGU on
#     its reset divisors at 491.52 MHz -- HALF the clock every budget assumes.
#     Read off the running window pair on 2026-09-09: CGU0_CTL 0x00002800 on
#     both chips, which is the reset row, not the 983.04 row (0x00005000).
#
# The consequence was measured, not inferred: the shipping per-sample block-8
# image misses 75.1 % of blocks on chip 1 and 70.9 % on chip 2, and a half
# that is not rewritten is transmitted again, so the wire carries stale whole
# blocks. No capacity number, latency figure or family walk could see it,
# because they were all taken on a different build.
#
# So the parameters that decide whether the loop fits the block live HERE, and
# nowhere else. `./build.sh` reads this file, `tools/dsp/dsp_codegen.py` reads
# this file for DSP4_GEN_BLOCK, and build.sh REFUSES to build a source tree
# whose generated dsp_block.h disagrees with it. An environment variable still
# overrides any line here -- that is how the control arms are built -- but the
# override is then explicit, in one command, and shows up in the image's own
# DIAG_BUILD_CFG word.
#
# FORMAT: KEY=VALUE, one per line, '#' comments. Parsed by shell (`source`)
# and by Python (tools/dsp/build_config.py). Values must be plain integers.

# ---- the four that decide whether the block loop fits the block ----

# Samples per DMA block. The whole tree is generated from this: every loop
# count, slot array, DMA ring, ramp step, meter coefficient and verdict rate.
# PW ruling 2026-09-03. Changing it means regenerating the tree, not editing
# dsp_block.h -- see tools/dsp/dsp_codegen.py.
DSP4_GEN_BLOCK=16

# One call per node per block with the sample loop inside the kernel, instead
# of one call per node per sample. Chip 1 330,389 -> 134,325 cycles/block,
# chip 2 286,757 -> 170,622, measured 2026-09-09 at block 8.
DSP4_BLOCK_KERNELS=1

# The ping/pong phase fix (src/sport_init.asm). The core used to start on the
# half the DDE was already clocking out, so every transmitted window was
# spliced from two or three consecutive blocks. 100.0000 % ordered on the part
# with it, 33 % without.
DSP4_BLK_LATCH=1

# Core clock. 983 = 983.040 MHz, legal on the ADSP-21564KSWZ10 fitted at
# U5/U6 (PW read the marking 2026-08-24) and OUT OF SPEC on a KSWZ8. This is
# the clock every cycle budget on this project is quoted at; a build with 0
# runs at 491.52 MHz and has half the budget it is being scored against.
DSP4_CCLK_TARGET=983

# ---- the rest of the shipping configuration, stated so it is not implicit ----

DSP4_BISECT=0             # 0 = production; anything else PARKS the firmware
DSP4_BLOCK_MASK=7         # 1 scatter | 2 node graph | 4 gather; 7 = whole loop
DSP4_CHAN_MASK=1          # CFG_CHAN_MASK/CFG_AUX_MASK have readers: a D24 runs 24 strips
DSP4_SCOPE_GATE=1         # skip nodes scoped to the other product at the dispatch table
DSP4_BQ_FLOAT=1           # the float landing, 2026-09-03
DSP4_BQ_ROUNDONCE=1       # per-stage saturate deleted, error feedback kept (PW, 2026-09-02)
# DSP4_BQ_GUARD is DERIVED, not set: dsp_block.h forces it to 0 whenever
# DSP4_BQ_FLOAT is on, because the float cascades are guard-free. Setting it
# here would be a line that does not describe the image -- the part read back
# 0 with this file saying 1, which is exactly the check DIAG_BUILD_CFG is for.
# ---- the two switches the capacity record was quoting and this file
# ---- did not name (findings S11-1, settled S12)
#
# THE RULE THIS FILE EXISTS FOR APPLIED TO ITSELF. Every capacity figure
# from 2026-09-01 to 2026-09-09 was taken by the profile scripts, which
# force both of these to 1; build.sh defaults both to 0; this file named
# neither. Read against the shipping pair the two instruments disagreed by
# 78,245 cycles/block on chip 2 at D24 and 108,331 at D32 -- 24 % and 33 %
# of budget -- and the record could not say which number was the product
# (S10-6). They are named here now, at the value the image that SHIPS is
# built with, so that gap can never reopen: an arm that wants them on says
# so on its command line and the image's own DIAG_BUILD_CFG2 word says so
# back.
#
# WHAT THEY ARE WORTH, measured on the part 2026-09-09, D32 all-ones mask:
# together they take chip 2 from 112.7 % of budget to 82.03 % avg /
# 86.75 % worst with zero missed blocks over 270,082 -- D32 FITS with them
# and does not without. STRIP_FUSED alone is 3,542 cycles (1.08 %) and is
# PROVEN (famverify verdict-for-verdict identical to shipping, three
# numeric arms BIT_EXACT). SIMD_DYN is the other 97,092 cycles (29.6 %).
#
# Turning either of them on for the product is PW's ruling, not this
# file's: see MW/D32/DSP/dsp4-simd-dyn-s12-20260909.md for the decision
# table and what still stands against SIMD_DYN.

# Fused strip kernels -- intermediates kept in registers and the MAC
# accumulator instead of round-tripping through memory. Block-kernel
# builds only.
DSP4_STRIP_FUSED=0

# Paired (SIMD) dynamics and biquads: GATE/COMP -- and, through the
# derived DSP4_BQ_PAIRED_GRAPH / DSP4_C2_BQ_PAIRED_GRAPH, FILT/EQ and
# chip 2's aux and main biquads -- run two channels in one instruction
# stream. Also wires the odd block pool and the pair-ordered chain.
DSP4_SIMD_DYN=0

# Chip 2's AUX and MAIN biquads paired (derived: only takes effect when
# DSP4_SIMD_DYN is on, through DSP4_C2_BQ_PAIRED_GRAPH). NAMED HERE AT 0
# BECAUSE IT IS NOT AUDIO-CORRECT, measured on the part 2026-09-09
# (findings S12-5): with it on, a band gain written into a paired AUX GEQ
# and a notch gain written into a paired AUX AFB do not reach the audio --
# the injected step comes out of the node bit-unchanged in both the low
# and the high coefficient state, and both families read INERT where the
# same image with this at 0 reads them LIVE. Chip 1's pairing
# (DSP4_BQ_GRAPH) and chip 2's paired DYNAMICS are clean.
#
# It is 0 here rather than absent so that turning DSP4_SIMD_DYN on in this
# file cannot silently ship that defect. It costs capacity: see the
# decision table in MW/D32/DSP/dsp4-simd-dyn-s12-20260909.md.
#
# NOTE, and it is the same shape as the fault this file exists for:
# DIAG_BUILD_CFG2 does NOT carry this bit, so the two candidate images
# read back the same word and differ in audio. Recorded as S12-7.
DSP4_C2_BQ_GRAPH=0

# ---- S9-2 Option A, ADOPTED (PW ruling 2026-09-09 14:3x) ----
#
# Transmit a half early. The core fills the DMA half the DDE is NOT
# clocking, so a block's outputs are complete a whole period before frame 0
# of that half goes on the wire; this removes the deadline rather than
# buying margin against it. Measured on the part 2026-09-09 (S11,
# `dsp4-s92-optionA-20260909.md`): 100.0000 % ordered at full load with the
# Pi staircase, ONE entry in the histogram, for ZERO cycles and ZERO DM --
# there is no staging block, the core writes the half it is not clocking.
#
# A PER-CHIP MASK because the cost is per chip: 1 = chip 1's inter-chip TX,
# 2 = chip 2's converter TX, 3 = both. PW ruled CHIP 2 ONLY. It costs
# +16 samples of output latency, so the through-DSP figure is 82 samples /
# 1.708 ms at block 16 and that is the contract number -- see the window
# note. Chip 1's inter-chip TX still has the same defect and the stamp
# cannot see it; that is recorded, not fixed.
#
# Requires DSP4_BLK_LATCH (src/sport_init.asm says so at assembly time) and
# DSP4_GATHER_FIRST stays on beside it -- with GATHER_FIRST off the same arm
# reads 98.2156 % and chip 2 misses 2.7 % of blocks.
DSP4_TX_EARLY=2

DSP4_TXPROBE=0            # bench instrument only; never in a shipping image
DSP4_PROFILE_SIGNAL=0     # measurement arm only
